{"nodes": [{"id": "android", "label": "ANDROID.md \u2014 Android runbook", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runbook for the Capacitor 8 build sideloaded on a Galaxy S25: toolchain, build, signing, install, data migration, updates, emulator smoke tests and known limitations."}, {"id": "android_capacitor_wrapper", "label": "Capacitor 8 Android wrapper (same React codebase)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "android/ + src/native/ wrap the unchanged React app for a sideloaded Samsung Galaxy S25 (One UI 8.5 / Android 16); the GitHub Pages PWA keeps deploying from main."}, {"id": "android_permanent_identity", "label": "Permanent identity: appId, https://localhost origin, release key", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "appId io.github.monniale.gymtracker, origin https://localhost (no server block in capacitor.config.ts) and the release key are fixed: changing any of them means a new app with empty storage, so every workout on the phone is lost."}, {"id": "android_toolchain", "label": "Android toolchain (Node \u2265 22, JDK 21 with javac, SDK 36)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "@capacitor/cli 8.5.2 needs Node \u2265 22 while the PWA still builds on Node 18+; the distro JRE lacks javac so Temurin 21 is used; env.sh sets ANDROID_HOME and PATH; a udev rule grants Samsung USB access."}, {"id": "android_dual_build_outputs", "label": "Dual build outputs: dist/ (Pages PWA) vs dist-android/", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "npm run build produces the Pages PWA (base /GymTracker/, service worker) checked by check-pwa-dist.mjs; build:android produces dist-android/ with base ./ and no service worker or manifest; cap:sync copies it into android assets."}, {"id": "android_release_pipeline", "label": "Guarded release build (release.sh)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only way to build for the phone: refuses on uncommitted tracked files, a versionCode lower than the last release, or a synced live-reload server block / inspectable WebView; runs npm test, signs v2+v3+v4 and verifies with apksigner, zipalign -P 16 and aapt2. npx cap build android is banned (v1-only signatures rejected by targetSdk 36); an inspectable release exposes the PAT and Gemini key over USB."}, {"id": "android_versioning_scheme", "label": "Versioning: versionName = package.json version, versionCode = git commit count", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "versionCode = git rev-list --count HEAD (override with GT_VERSION_CODE / -PgtVersionCode); an update needs a versionCode \u2265 the installed one."}, {"id": "android_live_reload", "label": "Live reload (debug builds only)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "npx cap run android -l changes the WebView origin, so it is for debug builds only, and cap:sync must be re-run afterwards because a release build fails on a leftover server block."}, {"id": "android_signing_key_backup", "label": "Release signing key backup", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "gymtracker-release.jks + keystore.properties in ~/.android-keys/gymtracker/ must be backed up offline: without the same key an update cannot install and the only way out is an uninstall that deletes all phone data. .gitignore blocks *.jks, *.keystore and keystore.properties."}, {"id": "android_sideload_install", "label": "Sideload install on the Galaxy S25", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Auto Blocker off, USB debugging on, adb install -r of the release APK (or install from My Files); Play Protect may ask for a scan. The app declares no SMS, accessibility or notification-listener permissions."}, {"id": "android_data_migration", "label": "PWA \u2192 app data migration", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The app's https://localhost storage is separate from the PWA's monniale.github.io origin, so it starts empty: finish workouts, sync and export in the PWA, then Connect GitHub Sync choosing 'Use cloud data (replace this device)' or import the JSON backup. Never 'Merge both' on a fresh install: freshly seeded settings and exercises would win and overwrite the real ones everywhere."}, {"id": "android_notification_setup", "label": "One UI notification setup", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Allow notifications, Battery \u2192 Unrestricted, add GymTracker to Never sleeping apps, optionally Live notifications, then test with the phone locked via Test rest (15 s) and Send test reminder (15 s)."}, {"id": "android_update_flow", "label": "Update flow (commit \u2192 release.sh \u2192 adb install -r)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Needs the same signing key and a versionCode \u2265 the installed one; never uninstall, as that deletes all data."}, {"id": "android_debug_sync_isolation", "label": "Debug builds never use the real sync repo", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A debug build is a separate app (\u2026.debug) but pushes test data to whatever repo it is connected to, so it uses a throwaway repo and PAT; smoke.sh aborts when the debug app is connected to gymtracker-data."}, {"id": "android_s25_avd", "label": "S25-like emulator AVD (360 CSS px)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "1080 px at 480 dpi = 360 CSS px, kept in the gitignored .android-test/, reproduces the Galaxy S25 viewport for the smoke test."}, {"id": "android_smoke_test", "label": "Emulator smoke test (checks 1\u201310)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "smoke.sh reinstalls the debug APK and checks cold launch, origin/platform/no SW, 360/320 px layout + font scale, insets, channels, exact alarms, rest timer fg/bg, process death, reminders planned/fired/tap-routed and the back button; cdp-eval.mjs evaluates JS in the debug WebView."}, {"id": "android_semi_manual_checks", "label": "Semi-manual checks (11\u201316 + on-device)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shade +15 s/Skip, keep-awake on /workout/session, export share sheet, import + re-plan, update/reboot keeping data and re-arming reminders, Doze firing; on the S25: ML Kit scanner, Live Update chip, edge-to-edge insets and the rest alert on earbuds/vibrate."}, {"id": "android_rolling_reminder_horizon", "label": "Rolling reminder horizon vs Samsung sleeping apps", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One UI sleeps apps unused ~3 days (alarms restricted) and deep-sleeps them after ~16, so reminders are planned only a few days ahead (7 days; water 2; one recap) with an 'Open GymTracker to keep your reminders coming' notice on the last planned day; after a reboot reminders re-arm only after the first unlock."}, {"id": "android_resume_driven_work", "label": "Nothing runs while the app is closed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sync, daily rank checks and re-planning happen only on open/resume; only already-scheduled alarms and rest-timer actions fire, and notification taps only navigate, never write data."}, {"id": "android_rest_timer_limitations", "label": "Native rest timer limitations", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The 'Rest over' alert needs notifications allowed (in-app beep + vibration otherwise); a swiped countdown re-posts on resume because the end alarm is re-armed; the Live Update chip is unverified on One UI 8.5; exact timing relies on USE_EXACT_ALARM."}, {"id": "android_text_zoom_pinned", "label": "WebView text zoom pinned to 100%", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The One UI font size does not apply inside the app, keeping the 360/320 px layouts intact."}, {"id": "android_barcode_fallback", "label": "ML Kit scanner with zxing fallback", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ML Kit downloads its scanner module through Play services on first use; if that fails, the zxing camera fallback and manual entry remain."}, {"id": "android_backup_policy", "label": "Backup policy: allowBackup=false; GitHub Sync + JSON export", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Android cloud backup is off to keep the PAT and Gemini key out of Google Drive; storage.persist() is best effort and uninstalling deletes everything, so GitHub Sync and JSON export are the backups."}], "edges": [{"source": "android", "target": "android_capacitor_wrapper", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "android", "target": "android_permanent_identity", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "android", "target": "android_toolchain", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "android", "target": "android_dual_build_outputs", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "ANDROID.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "android", "target": "android_release_pipeline", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score":